module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.KeyLemma.MilnorKDegreeOne
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.KeyLemma.MilnorKDegreeTwo
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.Symbols.Reciprocity
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.Symbols.SteinbergTame

/-!
# The tame-symbol boundary on Milnor K₂ and the vanishing of the composite

Stacks 0GU9 claims that for `(S, δ)` as in Stacks 02QL, `X` locally of finite type over `S` and
`k ∈ ℤ`, the three locally finite groups

`⨁'_{δ(x) = k + 2} K₂ᴹ(κ(x)) ⟶ ⨁'_{δ(x) = k + 1} K₁ᴹ(κ(x)) ⟶ ⨁'_{δ(x) = k} K₀ᴹ(κ(x))`

form a complex. Here `Kᴹ` is Milnor K-theory (Stacks 0EAY), the primed sum is the subgroup of
locally finite families (Stacks 0GU2), the second differential is the divisor differential of
Stacks 0GU3, and the first differential sends a family `ξ = ∑ₓ αₓ` to the family whose
coefficient at `x'` is `∑_{x ⇝ x'} ∂_{𝒪_{Wₓ, x'}}(αₓ)`, where `Wₓ` is the integral closed
subscheme with generic point `x` and `∂` is the tame symbol of Stacks 02Q1.

The source's argument for `∂ ∘ ∂ = 0` is this. Fix `x''` with `δ(x'') = k`. Local finiteness and
additivity reduce the coefficient of `x''` in `∂(∂(ξ))` to a single `αₓ` with `δ(x) = k + 2`, and
linearity reduces that to a pure symbol `f ⊗ g`. Writing `W` for the integral closed subscheme
with generic point `x`, the coefficient vanishes outright when `x'' ∉ W`, and in the remaining
case equals

`∑_{x ⇝ x' ⇝ x'', δ(x') = k + 1} ord_{𝒪_{closure {x'}, x''}}(∂_{𝒪_{W, x'}}(f, g))`.

The two-dimensional local ring `A = 𝒪_{W, x''}` has fraction field `κ(x)`, its height-one primes
`𝔮` are the intermediate points `x'`, and `A_𝔮 = 𝒪_{W, x'}`, `A / 𝔮 = 𝒪_{closure {x'}, x''}`; so
the displayed sum is the one the key algebraic lemma of Stacks 0EAX sets to zero.

This file carries out that argument in its local algebraic form, for a two-dimensional
Noetherian local domain. Two things are proved. First, the tame symbol of a one-dimensional
Noetherian local domain, a bimultiplicative pairing on the units of its fraction field, is
descended to a homomorphism out of the degree-two Milnor K-group: the pairing is read additively,
lifted over the tensor square, and the Steinberg relation of Stacks 02Q9 shows it kills the
Steinberg submodule, so it factors through the presentation of `K₂ᴹ` by that quotient. This is
the local component of the source's first differential. Second, summing the orders of those
boundaries over the height-one primes of a two-dimensional Noetherian local domain gives zero,
for *every* class of `K₂ᴹ` of the fraction field and not merely for a pure symbol: this is the
source's reduction "by additivity, by linearity" carried out in full, with the pure-symbol case
supplied by Stacks 0EAX and the general case following by an induction over
the presentation of `K₂ᴹ`, the sum staying finite at each step because the tame symbol is trivial
at all but finitely many height-one primes.

## Deviations from the source

* The fraction field of the two-dimensional local domain `A` is realized as `FractionRing A` in
  the reciprocity statement, rather than as an arbitrary `K` with `IsFractionRing A K`. The
  boundary at a height-one prime `𝔮` is built from the tame symbol of `A_𝔮`, which needs `K` to
  be a fraction field of `A_𝔮` as well, and the development has no transport of Milnor K-groups
  along an isomorphism of fields with which to move an arbitrary `K` into that position. The
  construction of the boundary itself is stated for an arbitrary fraction field.
* Only the local algebraic core of the tag is formalized. The geometric indexing of the sum --
  the identification of the height-one primes of `𝒪_{W, x''}` with the intermediate points `x'`,
  and of `A_𝔮`, `A / 𝔮` with the local rings there -- the locally finite chain groups in degrees
  `k + 2`, `k + 1`, `k`, the assembly of the first differential out of its local components, and
  the resulting three-term complex are *not* formalized here.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.milnorKTwoTameSymbol` is the tame symbol of a one-dimensional Noetherian
  local domain as a homomorphism from the degree-two Milnor K-group of its fraction field to the
  degree-one Milnor K-group of its residue field.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.milnorKTwoPureSymbol` is the pure symbol `{f, g}` in the degree-two Milnor
  K-group of a field.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.localMilnorBoundary` is that boundary at a height-one prime of a
  two-dimensional Noetherian local domain, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.localMilnorBoundaryOrder` the order of its value along the quotient.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.milnorKTwoTameSymbol_pureSymbol`: the boundary sends the pure symbol
  `{f, g}` to the tame symbol of `f` and `g`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.milnorKTwo_induction`: the degree-two Milnor K-group is generated by pure
  symbols.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.sum_localMilnorBoundaryOrder_eq_zero`: the orders of the Milnor K₂
  boundaries at the height-one primes of a two-dimensional Noetherian local domain sum to zero.

